IMPORT prelude

-- Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not
-- the daydate library. The Act's counted periods are: 45 business days after a complaint to the public entity
-- (s 65(1)(b)); 1 year after the alleged contravention (s 70(1)(d)); 5 years after an override provision commences
-- (s 45(2)). Its commencement is "a day to be fixed by proclamation" (s 2); the proclamation is not deposited, so
-- whether something happened before the commencement is asked, never computed.
--
-- "Business day" is not defined in this Act. It is the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) term, which is not deposited;
-- the reading taken (fork F1 in NOTES.md) is a day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday, with the public
-- holidays supplied by the person as a list of dates.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Human Rights Act 2019`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `first` `is on or before` `second` IF DATE_SERIAL `first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `second`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `first` `is before` `second` IF DATE_SERIAL `first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `second`

-- A Gregorian leap year.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

-- The same day and month n years on; for 29 February, when that year is not a leap year, 28 February (fork F2).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary` `n` `years after` `the start` MEANS
    IF     (DATE_DAY `the start` EQUALS 29)
       AND (DATE_MONTH `the start` EQUALS 2)
       AND (NOT (`leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `n`)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `n`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the start`) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `n`)

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Business days (fork F1)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- 1 is Monday ... 5 is Friday, 6 is Saturday, 0 is Sunday (DATE_SERIAL of Monday 9 November 2026 is 1 modulo 7).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekday number of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a business day` `the day` `the public holidays` IF
        `the weekday number of` `the day` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the weekday number of` `the day` AT MOST 5
    AND (NOT (elem (DATE_SERIAL `the day`) (map DATE_SERIAL `the public holidays`)))

-- The n-th business day after a day (the day itself not counted); n of 0 or less gives the day itself.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE, `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the business day after` `n` `the day` `the public holidays` MEANS
    IF `n` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `is a business day` `the next day` `the public holidays`
         THEN `the business day after` (`n` MINUS 1) `the next day` `the public holidays`
         ELSE `the business day after` `n` `the next day` `the public holidays`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS 1 `days after` `the day`
